Why do we need a separate owned_tensor_indices list for the receive path, while the send path iterates over tensor_to_owner? They seem like two sides of the same operation. Could we combine them into something like this?

```
for tensor, owner in tensor_to_owner.items():
    if owner == local_rank:
        # Copy our local shard and receive the others.
    else:
        # Send our shard to the owner, if we have one.
```

